Filetype: IR signals file
Version: 1
#
# Denon DRA-395 stereo receiver
#
# Denon protocol (the Sharp-derived 15-bit format), device 12 -- the generic Denon *stereo
# receiver* code set (irdb codes/Denon/Receiver/12,-1.csv). Decoders report this as Denon.
# Denon's classic AVR sets sit on device 8 and newer AVRs use 48-bit Denon-K, so AVR codes do
# not work on this model.
#
# GENERATED from that published table and CONFIRMED on the actual unit 2026-08-21 with a
# Global Cache iTach IP2IR, watching the front panel one command at a time. Nothing here was
# learned/captured from a remote -- all signals were generated, then verified by transmitting.
#
# Power_on, Speaker_A and Speaker_B had no published captures of the device-12 versions that I
# could find (checked LIRC's Denon remotes, this repo, and RemoteCentral -- whose Denon speaker
# discretes are the newer Denon-K AVR codes, a different protocol). All three verified working.
# Power_off, Vol_up, Vol_dn, Mute and Input_Vaux confirmed on the unit as well; Vol_dn was sent
# ten times at 0.5 s spacing and all ten landed. The remaining Input_* come from the same table
# and are untested here.
#
# NOTE on Denon_DRA_365R.ir in this folder: its "A B channels" button is NOT speaker A/B. It
# decodes to device 4, function 83 -- irdb lists that as DECK SELECT A/B -- and sits with that
# remote's FF/RR/Record/Play transport buttons. The DRA-365R has no built-in cassette deck;
# those drive a companion Denon deck. Speaker_A / Speaker_B below are the receiver's real
# speaker-output toggles on device 12.
#
# Both speaker outputs off makes the front panel read "H/P only", which is a handy
# way to verify these without any audio playing.
#
#
